# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DealFinder AI — end-to-end database (template)
#
# Copy to `.env.e2e`, or better, let `npm run db:e2e:prepare` write it for you —
# the port is allocated by `prisma dev` and is not predictable (see below).
#
# Read only by `playwright.config.ts`, which passes it to the API it starts *and*
# applies it to the Playwright worker itself. Nothing else loads this file, and
# `.env` is untouched: the long-lived development database keeps the demo
# catalogue you actually browse.
#
# ── Why the suite has its own database ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# The shared `prisma dev` instance degraded under sustained end-to-end load. The
# daemon began terminating connections mid-suite and then exited outright, which
# surfaced as `Connection terminated unexpectedly`, a page rendering its shell
# with an empty `<main>`, and `Timed out waiting 120000ms from config.webServer`.
# None of that is an assertion failure and all of it reads like one.
#
# A dedicated instance gives the suite its own storage, its own query-insights
# stream and its own lifecycle, so a suite run can no longer take the development
# database down with it.
#
# ── This database is disposable ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Treat it as test infrastructure, not data. It is meant to be thrown away and
# rebuilt — `npx prisma dev rm dealfinder-e2e --force` then
# `npm run db:e2e:prepare` — and it must never share state with the development
# database. That disposability is the point: the development database cannot be
# reset (see docs/database-environment.md), this one can.
#
# ── The port is machine-specific ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `prisma dev` IGNORES --port/--db-port/--shadow-db-port in the installed version
# (v0.16.27) and auto-allocates the next free block per instance. So the port
# below is whatever it happened to assign, is not portable, and must never be
# hard-coded in committed code. `npm run db:e2e:prepare` reads the real value
# back from the instance's own metadata. To check by hand:
#
#   npx prisma dev ls
#
# `.env.e2e` itself is gitignored (`.env.*`), which is why only this template is
# committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Instance: dealfinder-e2e. Replace the port with the allocated one.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:51218/template1?sslmode=disable"

# Local Prisma Postgres is PGlite-backed: it accepts one active connection at a
# time and queues the rest. Stays 1 unless the database itself proves otherwise.
DATABASE_POOL_MAX=1
